    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d626">

                <pb facs="1289" n="1277" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg1277"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of Staff</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Eisenhower</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to General Marshall</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-07-02">2 July 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>93274. Recent press reports from Shanghai, repeated here, relative to General
                        Wedemeyer’s<anchor n="35" xml:id="d626-f1"/> impending return to China imply
                    your early return to the United States. In the belief that this may be
                    embarrassing to you in your present negotiations I am prepared to relieve
                    Wedemeyer of assignment to China and re-assign him to the Continental US,
                    without in any way prejudicing future plans. Wedemeyer concurs. Please
                    advise.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d626-f1" n="35" xml:id="d626-f1-content">
                <p>Lt. Gen. Albert C. Wedemeyer, until April Commanding General, U. S. Forces, China
                    Theater.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
